Help For The Receive Audio Setup

Receive audio setup: full stop next input; comma previous; c cycles physical input channels. v checks the selected channel level for one second without playing it. Enter saves the choice; q returns to the decoder menu without saving. h help. No input opens until you request v; Enter validates supported format without capture. Device names and host audio system are announced. Several entries may refer to the same physical input through different host systems. Choose the radio, not your microphone. The level check only detects audio; it cannot prove which device is the radio. Receive a steady signal and compare levels/channels. Channel numbers do not guarantee Main/Sub. Saved name and host must uniquely match on later use; missing or duplicate devices fail without fallback. Setup never changes Windows defaults, screen-reader output or playback devices. Opening and browsing leave existing capture running. An explicit v check or Enter save releases active audio CW capture first; restart it explicitly afterwards. If no saved input is available, this is reported; use full stop/comma or c to select a candidate before checking or saving. Optional sounddevice/PortAudio is required. Changes are saved only with Enter; q does not save your current browsing choice.

